1.	Start the game with energy set to 100. All clues and suspects start locked. The starting location is Backstage.
2.	Show the introduction, explain the case, and wait for the player to press Enter.
3.	Begin the main loop.
4.	Show the player’s current energy, current location, and the actions they can choose.
5.	Take the player's input.
6.	If the player chooses to search location:
 •	Check the current location.
 •	If its clue has not been found yet, give the clue, unlock the related suspect, and ask the small puzzle or question.
 •	If the answer is wrong, reduce energy.
 •	If the clue was already found, inform the player and reduce energy.
7.	If the player chooses to move to another location:
 •	Show all possible locations.
 •	Change the current location based on the player’s choice.
8.	If the player chooses to talk to a suspect:
 •	Only allow this if the suspect has been unlocked.
 •	Show their dialogue and mark them as “talked.”
9.	After each action, check if all three clues have been found and all three suspects have been talked to. If yes, start the final accusation.
10.	In the final accusation, let the player choose the culprit. If the choice is correct, the game ends with a win. If it is wrong, reduce energy and continue if possible.
11.	The game ends either when the player’s energy becomes 0 or when they correctly identify the culprit.
